      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Gethinctho">Geþyncðo</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="458" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif man gehádedum oððe ælþeodigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ahwar gederede wórdes oððe weorces, þonne gebyrede biscpe ⁊ cynge, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> betan, swa hi raðost mihton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="458" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hit gewurde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man gehadedu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oððe ælþeodigum ahwar gederode wordes oððe weorces, þonne gebyrede cinge ⁊ bisceope, þæt hig þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> bettan, swa hig raþost mihton.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="459" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si eueniret, ut ordinatus uel alienigena distraheretur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.9-2"/> alicubi uerbis uel operibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, tunc pertinebat regi et episcopo hoc emendare, quam citius possent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.11-2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-in"><pb n="459" ed="#liebermann"/>[63, 1] Et si contigerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.8"/>, aliquem nocuisse ordinato<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.9"/> aut peregrino, tunc rex et episcopus iuste, quam citius possent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.10"/>, hoc deberent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.11"/> emendare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.12"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="12" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hit gewurde þæt man gehadedum oððe ælþeodigum ahwar gederode wordes oððe weorces, þonne gebyrede cinge and bisceope þæt hig þæt bettan swa hig raþost mihton.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="459" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.de.a"/> geschah, dass jemand einem Geweihten oder Fremden irgendwo in Wort oder That Schaden zufügte, dann gebührte dem König<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.de1.b"/> und Bischof<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.de.1"/>, dass sie so schnell sie konnten [den Thäter] dies büssen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Gethyn_8.lnote.de.2"/> liessen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if it happened that someone did harm to an ordained man or a stranger anywhere in word or deed, then it was for the king and the bishop to make [the offender] atone for it as quickly as they could.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="477" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone, anywhere, injured an ecclesiastic or a stranger by word or deed, then it was the concern of the bishop and the king, that they should atone for it as quickly as they could.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h">And if it so happened anywhere that someone injured one in orders or a stranger by word or deed, then it was the responsibility of the king and the bishop to remedy it as swiftly as they could.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="459"><ref target="clause:IICn_40">II Cn 40</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 40</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Had_1-2">Had 1.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><ref target="clause:IICn_40">II Cn 40</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">D has ‘bishop and king’ in that order. In H, Norðleod follows. Liebermann compares II Cn 40.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hit . . . þæt: omitted D</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">458</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Norðleoda laga</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Norðleoda laga follows</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">458</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Northleod</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Northleod follows</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tingeret <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tingeret Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tum aut peregrinum <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tum aut peregrinum Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-sunt <hi rend="italic">HRl;</hi> -sit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-sunt HRl; -sit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bent <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> e. d. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bent H; e. d. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Ine</hi> 58 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi>, <hi rend="italic">oben S.</hi> 115†</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ine 58 f. follows, above p. 115†</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disturbaretur <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disturbaretur R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">opibus <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">opibus MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Mirce</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Mirce follows</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.de.a" n="a" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">259</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Z. 1 = Had 1, 2.—Längere Form ist gegen D durch hq I als archetyp erwiesen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">L. 1 = Had 1, 2.—The longer form is proved by hq I, against D, to be that of the archetype</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">459</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lq = <hi rend="italic">Vorlage von</hi> Ld <hi rend="italic">und</hi> Quadr.; hlq = <hi rend="italic">Vorlage von</hi> H <hi rend="italic">und</hi> lq</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lq = exemplar of Ld and Quadr.; hlq = exemplar of H and lq</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">259</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bischof 9q; Schutz über Fremde (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7ff.), diesem, wie schon in EGu, aber nicht Atr oder Cn, beigelegt, spricht für hierarchische Tendenz. D stellt den Bischof dem König voran, ebenfalls hierarchisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bischof 9q; protection over foreigners (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7ff.), assigned to him, as already in EGu but not in Atr or Cn, points to a hierarchical tendency. D puts the bishop before the king, likewise hierarchical</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Gethyn_8.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">259</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘gutmachen, zur (Ordnung) Sühne bringen’, auch Iudex 2, nicht immer durch eigenes Opfer; z. B. <hi rend="italic">fæhðe gebetan</hi>: ‘Totschlag rächen’ Beowulf 2465; <hi rend="italic">audire</hi> von Gott, der Klagen erhört, Deut. 1, 17 übs. Ælfric <hi rend="italic">betan</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘make good, bring to (order) atonement’, also Iudex 2, not always by one’s own sacrifice; e.g. <hi rend="italic">fæhðe gebetan</hi>: ‘avenge a homicide’ Beowulf 2465; Ælfric translates <hi rend="italic">audire</hi>, said of God who hears complaints, Deut. 1, 17, by <hi rend="italic">betan</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
